  "helpFaqLeaveQ": "What if someone disconnects or leaves?",
  "helpFaqLeaveA": "If a player leaves, the game goes on and their turn is skipped. If the host (whoever opened the game) leaves or is out of reach for more than 25 seconds, the game closes for everyone.",
  "helpFaqHostQ": "Who is the \"host\"?",
  "helpFaqHostA": "Whoever opened the game. Their phone is the referee: it runs the rules, deals secret roles and counts votes. The host plays like everyone else and never sees anyone else's secrets.",
  "helpFaqCheatQ": "Can anyone cheat?",
  "helpFaqCheatA": "In Battleships and Rock paper scissors your choice is locked with a fingerprint before the other player sees it, and the app catches anyone who changes it or lies. In the other games the host's phone is the referee.",
  "helpXoGoal": "Be the first to get three of your marks in a row — across, down or diagonally.",
  "helpXoHow": "The first player is ✕, the other ○.\nTake turns tapping an empty square.\nIf the board fills up with no three in a row, it's a draw.\nThe starting player switches every match.",
  "helpXoTips": "The centre is the strongest first move.\nIf the other player has two in a row, block them right away.",
  "helpConnect4Goal": "Be the first to line up four pieces of your colour.",
  "helpConnect4How": "The board has 7 columns and 6 rows.\nTap a column and your piece drops to the lowest empty spot.\nThe four can be across, down or diagonal.\nIf the board fills up with no four in a row, it's a draw.",
  "helpConnect4Tips": "The middle column gives you the most chances.\nWatch the diagonals; people often miss them.",
  "helpBattleshipGoal": "Sink all of the other player's ships before they sink yours.",
  "helpBattleshipHow": "Each player has an 8×8 sea with 4 ships: lengths 4, 3, 3 and 2.\nTap \"New layout\" until you like it, then \"Ready\".\nTake turns tapping a square in the other sea to fire.\nThe answer is miss ○, hit ✕ or sunk.\nA hit gives you another shot; a miss passes the turn.",
  "helpBattleshipTips": "After a hit, try the squares next to it.\nShips never touch, so everything around a sunk ship is water.\nYour fleet never leaves your phone; at the end the app checks that nobody lied.",
  "helpRpsGoal": "First to win two throws wins the match.",
  "helpRpsHow": "Pick rock ✊, paper ✋ or scissors ✌️.\nRock breaks scissors, scissors cut paper, paper wraps rock.\nBoth picks are shown together once you have both chosen.\nSame pick? The throw is replayed.",
  "helpRpsTips": "Nobody can see your pick before choosing; the app locks it with a fingerprint.",
  "helpDotsGoal": "Claim the most boxes.",
  "helpDotsHow": "Take turns drawing a line between two neighbouring dots.\nWhoever draws the fourth side of a box claims it.\nClose a box and you play again.\nWhen every box is closed, the one with the most wins.",
  "helpDotsTips": "Avoid drawing the third side of a box; the next player takes it.\nNear the end, give away short chains and keep the long ones.",
  "helpMemoryGoal": "Collect the most matching pairs.",
  "helpMemoryHow": "All cards are face down; every picture appears twice.\nOn your turn flip two cards.\nIf they match you keep them and go again.\nIf not, they flip back after a moment and the next player goes.\nWhen the cards run out, whoever has the most pairs wins.",
  "helpMemoryTips": "Watch what the others flip; that's free information.",
  "helpSpyGoal": "Not the spy? Find them. The spy? Stay hidden, or work out the word.",
  "helpSpyHow": "The app picks a category (food, places…), and all the phones take part in dealing the roles and the word so nobody can cheat — not even whoever opened the game knows who the spy is.\nEveryone sees the word on their phone, except one player who sees \"You're the spy\" and the category only.\nIn turn, everyone gives a small hint about the word (out loud or typed) and taps \"Done\".\nAfter the hints, everyone votes for the spy.\nThe phone of the caught player shows their card: if they are the spy, they get one last chance to guess the word from the category.\nAt the end every phone reveals its secrets and checks that nobody cheated.",
  "helpSpyRoles": "🕵️ The spy: doesn't know the word and tries to act like they do.\n👤 Everyone else: knows the word and tries to unmask the spy without giving the word away.",
  "helpSpyTips": "Hints that are too obvious give the word to the spy; too vague and people suspect you.\nSpy: listen closely to the hints before yours.",
  "helpQuizGoal": "Answer right and fast to score the most points.",
  "helpQuizHow": "The host picks a category and the number of questions.\nEach question has 4 options and 15 seconds.\nA right answer earns 500 points, plus up to 500 for speed.\nAfter each question the right answer and the ranking are shown.",
  "helpQuizTips": "Time is measured on your own phone from the moment the question appears, so a slow network won't cost you points.",
  "helpMafiaGoal": "Town: find and vote out the mafia. Mafia: get rid of the town without being caught.",
  "helpMafiaHow": "The app deals roles in secret; everyone sees only their own.\nNight 🌙: the mafia pick a victim, the doctor protects someone, the detective checks someone.\nMorning ☀️: the app announces who was killed (or that the doctor saved them).\nDiscussion: 3 minutes to talk and accuse (the host can cut it short).\nVote: whoever gets the most votes is out and their role is revealed. A tie means nobody leaves.\nThen night again… until one side wins.",
  "helpMafiaRoles": "🔪 Mafia: about one per four players. They know each other and have a secret chat at night.\n💉 Doctor: protects someone each night (even themselves), but not the same person two nights running.\n🔍 Detective: learns each night whether someone is mafia.\n👤 Citizen: no power; their weapons are their wits and their vote.",
  "helpMafiaTips": "The town wins when every mafia member is out. The mafia win when they equal the rest.\nDead players watch and stay quiet.\nSitting together? Talk out loud; the app just keeps time and counts votes.",
