  "guideConnectTitle": "Ways to connect",
  "guideConnectIntro": "Wasl needs no internet, no SIM and no account. Pick a way to connect that suits where you are:",
  "guideWhat": "What it is",
  "guideWhen": "When to use it",
  "guideFacts": "Good to know",
  "guideHow": "How to start",
  "guideBtWhat": "Phones talk to each other directly over Bluetooth, with no network at all.",
  "guideBtWhen": "When there is no Wi-Fi and no hotspot: outdoors, on a trip, or when the network is down.",
  "guideBtFacts": "Range is about 10–30 m between two phones.\nEach phone links to about 5 others, and a message can hop up to 6 times, so it reaches much further.\nMessages, photos, files and voice notes. No video or calls (Bluetooth is too slow for them).",
  "guideBtHow": "Tap \"Bluetooth\" on the first screen.\nAllow the permissions (Bluetooth and nearby devices).\nPeople around you with Wasl open show up under \"Nearby\" by themselves.",
  "guideWifiWhat": "Phones on the same Wi-Fi, or one phone runs a hotspot and the others join it. The network does not need internet.",
  "guideWifiWhen": "When you share a home, hall or café, or when someone can turn on a hotspot.",
  "guideWifiFacts": "Much faster than Bluetooth, with video and voice / video calls.\nA hotspot usually takes 5 to 10 phones.\nSome public routers stop devices talking to each other; use a hotspot then.",
  "guideWifiHow": "Join a Wi-Fi network, or turn on a hotspot in your phone's settings and have your friends join it.\nTap \"Wi-Fi\" in Wasl.\nEveryone on the same network shows up by themselves.",
  "guideBothWhat": "Bluetooth and Wi-Fi together: your phone becomes a bridge between people on Wi-Fi and people on Bluetooth.",
  "guideBothWhen": "When people are spread out: some on a hotspot, some further away with only Bluetooth. Or to join two hotspots together.",
  "guideBothFacts": "The network grows: every phone on \"Both\" joins the two networks together.\nCalls and video stay inside one Wi-Fi network.\nIt uses a bit more battery.",
  "guideBothHow": "Join a Wi-Fi network or hotspot.\nTap \"Both\".\nWasl links everyone together by itself.",
  "guideMeshHops": "A message crosses at most 6 phones, and phones in between only pass it on; they can't read private chats.",
  "guideGroupsTitle": "Groups",
  "guideGamesTitle": "Games",
  "guideGamesBody": "In any chat tap 🎮 and pick a game. In a private chat your friend accepts and it starts; in a group, whoever wants to play taps \"Join\" and whoever opened it taps \"Start\". Tap any game below to see how it's played.",
