  "guideNetTitle": "Wasl network",
  "guideNetWhat": "Your phone starts its own Wi-Fi network from inside the app, with a random name and password and no internet. People next to you running Wasl get a \"Join\" button and are in with one tap; nobody types a password.",
  "guideNetWhen": "When there is no router: on a trip, outdoors, in a hall or at a party. Bluetooth is slow and there is no Wi-Fi, so Wasl makes one.",
  "guideNetFacts": "Each network takes about 5 to 10 phones. When there are more, someone else starts another one, and phones on \"Both\" link the networks over Bluetooth, so the network keeps growing with no router.\nStarting a network needs Android 8+, joining from the app Android 10+ (older phones join from Wi-Fi settings).\nSome phones drop their normal Wi-Fi while hosting.\nThe network closes when you close Wasl.",
  "guideNetHow": "Pick \"Both\" (so Bluetooth can pass the name and password to people next to you).\nUnder \"Nearby\" tap \"Start a Wasl network\".\nPeople next to you see \"Join\": they tap it and accept their phone's prompt.\nA phone can't join from inside Wasl? Tap \"Network QR\" and let them scan it with the camera.",
